00:39:35.970 --> 00:39:39.840
The machine is controlled
by the semiconductor.

00:39:39.840 --> 00:39:41.130
That's one thing.

00:39:41.130 --> 00:39:44.160
And the other thing is
what is called experience.

00:39:44.160 --> 00:39:49.110
Experience, that mean you
learn a lot of skill by years,

00:39:49.110 --> 00:39:51.810
and you have to remember, by the way.

00:39:51.810 --> 00:39:55.260
So I would say that if
you go to the hospital

00:39:55.260 --> 00:40:00.090
to see you got the flu,
so you tell the doctor,

00:40:00.090 --> 00:40:01.620
say, "I got the flu.

00:40:01.620 --> 00:40:04.500
I have coughing, I have a runny nose,

00:40:04.500 --> 00:40:06.840
and everything," blah, blah blah.

00:40:06.840 --> 00:40:09.360
And so the doctor will say,
"Okay, sit right there."

00:40:09.360 --> 00:40:12.660
Measure your temperature,
measure your heartbeat,

00:40:12.660 --> 00:40:17.660
and then be very patient
with you for half an hour,

00:40:19.470 --> 00:40:22.893
and then write down some medicine for you.

00:40:23.820 --> 00:40:25.410
I don't need it.

00:40:25.410 --> 00:40:30.410
I just using the AI to
collect all the flu example

00:40:31.680 --> 00:40:35.400
in this area, and then the
AI will make a judgment,

00:40:35.400 --> 00:40:40.400
say that what the age you
are, is a male or female,

00:40:41.580 --> 00:40:44.670
and what the symptom,
what kind of temperature,

00:40:44.670 --> 00:40:47.100
body temperature, what kind of heartbeat,

00:40:47.100 --> 00:40:49.680
what kind of blah blah blah.

00:40:49.680 --> 00:40:54.300
And then they also look
at, are you in New Haven,

00:40:54.300 --> 00:40:58.560
or you are in New York, or
you are in Washington, DC?

00:40:58.560 --> 00:41:02.280
And so the flu in that area of the people,

00:41:02.280 --> 00:41:04.380
the symptom look like what?

00:41:04.380 --> 00:41:07.620
And finally, get a conclusion

00:41:07.620 --> 00:41:10.680
and write down the medicine for you.

00:41:10.680 --> 00:41:15.270
And the accuracy will be 90 or 95%.

00:41:15.270 --> 00:41:17.370
So you don't need a doctor.

00:41:17.370 --> 00:41:19.851
You just type into the computer.

00:41:19.851 --> 00:41:20.684
(Jeff chuckles)

00:41:20.684 --> 00:41:24.810
And then 90 or 95% of accuracy,

00:41:24.810 --> 00:41:27.840
you still have 5% to 10%, right?

00:41:27.840 --> 00:41:29.550
Then you see a doctor.

00:41:29.550 --> 00:41:34.020
And then doctor say, "It's
not working for this one."

00:41:34.020 --> 00:41:36.870
And the computer ask, "So what years?"

00:41:36.870 --> 00:41:39.540
And then you type it into,

00:41:39.540 --> 00:41:42.990
so the computer continue to remember,

00:41:42.990 --> 00:41:46.350
continue to educate itself.

00:41:46.350 --> 00:41:50.820
And so finally, I don't
need a doctor to see

00:41:50.820 --> 00:41:52.920
when I have a flu.

00:41:52.920 --> 00:41:56.620
I don't need a doctor to
do the operation surgery.

00:42:00.150 --> 00:42:04.200
I don't need a doctor
to give me some advice,

00:42:04.200 --> 00:42:07.021
