00:43:08.630 --> 00:43:10.560
- First of all, thank
you for the great talk

00:43:10.560 --> 00:43:11.853
and inspiring us.

00:43:12.720 --> 00:43:17.700
Of course, every process in
the semiconductor manufacturing

00:43:17.700 --> 00:43:19.590
is very important.

00:43:19.590 --> 00:43:22.470
But first decade people talk a lot

00:43:22.470 --> 00:43:26.340
about miniaturizing the semiconductor

00:43:26.340 --> 00:43:29.370
and integrate more and
more chips inside of,

00:43:29.370 --> 00:43:32.730
more and more transistor
inside of the single chips.

00:43:32.730 --> 00:43:36.840
But it's like seven
nanometer, five nanometers,

00:43:36.840 --> 00:43:38.100
three nanometer, like that.

00:43:38.100 --> 00:43:43.100
But now, we will facing the
limit of the miniaturizing,

00:43:45.630 --> 00:43:48.030
the process.

00:43:48.030 --> 00:43:51.963
So what is your insight or prospect,

00:43:52.830 --> 00:43:56.220
which process will
attract people's attention

00:43:56.220 --> 00:44:00.153
after the miniaturizing and
integrating the transistors?

00:44:01.740 --> 00:44:02.613
- Good question.

00:44:03.574 --> 00:44:04.407
Is there any...

00:44:04.407 --> 00:44:06.210
Actually, your question should separate

00:44:06.210 --> 00:44:11.210
into, is there any
limitation at all, okay?

00:44:11.450 --> 00:44:15.107
And what we are doing to deal with it.

00:44:15.107 --> 00:44:17.070
I give you a story.

00:44:17.070 --> 00:44:21.793
When I graduated from
Yale, I joined TI in 19,

00:44:22.950 --> 00:44:26.310
actually, at the beginning of 1985.

00:44:26.310 --> 00:44:31.310
I graduated in 1985, but
I want to work quickly

00:44:33.630 --> 00:44:36.270
because I have a family to raise.

00:44:36.270 --> 00:44:40.950
So at the beginning of
the 1985, I work in TI.

00:44:40.950 --> 00:44:43.717
I read a paper published by IBM.

00:44:45.145 --> 00:44:48.720
They called it 1-micron technology.

00:44:48.720 --> 00:44:53.720
And they say, "Not for long
that will reach the limitation

00:44:55.230 --> 00:44:57.207
of the semiconductor device."

00:44:58.290 --> 00:44:59.850
If you look at it, look at it,

00:44:59.850 --> 00:45:02.537
look at the mean free
path of your electron

00:45:02.537 --> 00:45:04.350
at the kind of different temperature,

00:45:04.350 --> 00:45:08.010
you'll find out if a
channel length shorter

00:45:08.010 --> 00:45:12.548
than your mean free path,
there's a lot of limitation.

00:45:12.548 --> 00:45:14.343
There's a lot of high electron.

00:45:14.343 --> 00:45:17.310
There's a lot of physics inside.

00:45:17.310 --> 00:45:22.290
So they say, quickly,
.35 micron is the end

00:45:22.290 --> 00:45:25.770
of the semiconductor technology, okay?

00:45:25.770 --> 00:45:29.373
And since then, now today,
we are at three nanometer.

00:45:30.480 --> 00:45:34.860
And so the people ask me the
same thing we ask ourselves

00:45:34.860 --> 00:45:39.180
inside TSMC, "Is there any limitation?"

00:45:39.180 --> 00:45:42.210
So what happen after three nanometer?

00:45:42.210 --> 00:45:43.470
Do you know?

00:45:43.470 --> 00:45:45.000
Two nanometer.

00:45:45.000 --> 00:45:48.060
So what happened after two nanometer?

00:45:48.060 --> 00:45:50.310
1.4. I tell you the truth.

00:45:50.310 --> 00:45:52.920
You just time by .7 in one.

00:45:52.920 --> 00:45:57.920
And so one of the occasion
I answer the question,

00:46:00.870 --> 00:46:05.790
the people ask me, "What happen
after the 1.4 nanometer?"

00:46:05.790 --> 00:46:08.470
I say, "One nanometer."

00:46:08.470 --> 00:46:10.867
"And what happen after the one nanometer?"

00:46:10.867 --> 00:46:12.567
"Of course, .7."

00:46:13.440 --> 00:46:15.000
Something,
(audience chuckling)

00:46:15.000 --> 00:46:16.530
something like that.

00:46:16.530 --> 00:46:18.720
And they keep asking.

00:46:18.720 --> 00:46:21.570
And finally, my answer
is, "Why should I care?

00:46:21.570 --> 00:46:23.582
Because I retire already."

00:46:23.582 --> 00:46:25.494
(audience laughing)

00:46:25.494 --> 00:46:28.661
(audience applauding)

00:46:31.620 --> 00:46:35.926
- All right, thank you again, C.C.

00:46:35.926 --> 00:46:37.207
- Thank you, guys.
- A real pleasure.

00:46:37.207 --> 00:46:38.040
Thank you for coming.

00:46:38.040 --> 00:46:38.873
